6.1 Introduction

The Project Testing Phase verifies that the ComicCraft application works according to its functional and non-functional requirements. Testing is performed on individual modules and on the integrated application to identify errors and improve reliability.

6.2 Objectives of Testing

Verify that user inputs are accepted correctly.

Check the AI story-generation process.

Verify that comic illustrations are generated.

Ensure that images and narration are arranged in the correct order.

Test the PDF export functionality.

Identify and resolve errors.

Verify the overall user experience.

6.3 Types of Testing

1. Unit Testing

Individual functions such as generate_outline(), generate_story(), generate_image(), build_comic_layout(), and save_pdf() are tested separately.

2. Integration Testing

Checks whether the frontend, FastAPI backend, Gemini AI, image generator, layout builder, and PDF exporter work together correctly.

3. Functional Testing

Verifies that each feature performs the expected operation, including form submission, comic generation, preview display, and PDF export.

4. UI Testing

Checks whether input fields, buttons, images, and pages display correctly and whether the interface is easy to navigate.

5. Error Handling Testing

Tests the application's response to invalid inputs, unavailable APIs, image-generation errors, and PDF export failures.

6. Performance Testing

Measures the response time and resource usage of the application during comic generation, taking into account that AI services may have variable processing times.

